From b2bcf494adbecec85c1bcc4d83cb3b71f78e07e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:18:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): ci-flaky-cards accepts an overlap match as owner
 only when it is open and about the test, delivers cross-gateway comments via
 hermes-hub with read-back, and fails loud otherwise [daveey]

08811ca2f9d deferred every create_overlap refusal to the guard's first match. The guard
named three unrelated cards on gateway macbook (one done), the hub's hermes kanban could
not see them, the comment error was swallowed, 'appended' was logged, the wrong card was
recorded in state and the cron stayed ok: three live flakes were lost.

Now a match owns the flake only if it is open (status re-read from its owner; canonical
replica rows win over stale legacy rows) and its title/body names the test id (or its key
is deflake:<id>). Non-owners are passed back as --distinct-from with a reason naming the
test and the matched titles. A remote owner gets the comment through hermes-hub request
(deterministic request id, so a retry never double-posts) and it is read back from the
replica (or the owner's 'Comment added' receipt). Any delivery that fails or is not
confirmed logs FAILED, records nothing, leaves the GitHub run unprocessed for the next
poll and exits 1. Local comments are read back too, and a comment already on the card
for this job and test is not repeated. (t_01a189b2c78e9005)
